      "role": "user",
      "content": "That \"slippery and mischievous imp\" comment is a bit weird, but I guess I get the point about the difficulty. \n\nLet's focus on the technical side though. You mentioned L75.0 and L75.1, but those seem too narrow for what we're seeing. The presentations aren't just \"nodular\"; they are incredibly irregular, almost like the skin is being colonized by something growing in random, patchy, and jagged clusters. They have this very strange, uneven, knobby quality that doesn't follow any standard dermatological pattern. \n\nIs there a specific way within the ICD-10 hierarchy to code for these jagged, patchy, and disorganized eruptions when they appear almost as if they're growing in a chaotic or non-linear fashion? We need to move past just saying \"unspecified\" if the morphology is clearly something more distinct, even if it's anomalous.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
