      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's still a bit vague for our billing department. The issue is that \"unspecified\" is exactly what triggers the denials. If we use a code that basically says \"unspecified but with these descriptors,\" the insurance adjusters just reject it for lack of a definitive diagnosis. \n\nWhat I'm really looking for is how we classify these specific structural anomalies. When you have these jagged, uneven, almost parasitic-looking growths that appear in clusters and seem to have a life of their own because they are so disorganized, is there a high-level category for \"atypical growth patterns\" or \"disorganized structural dermatological anomalies\"? I need to know if there is any way to code the *nature* of the irregularity itself without it being lumped into a general \"unspecified\" category.",
